=== NOTE on the "GREEN: full unit suite" line above ===
That step was piped through `tail -3`, which cut the counts and left a bare exit
code 1. The cause is environmental and NOT a flake, and not K-012:
tests/unit/services/reports/incomeStatementDisclosureDb.test.ts skips itself when
DATABASE_URL is unset and runs against a real ledger when it is set. That step ran
in the same shell that had sourced the disposable zero-row fixture env for the
integration mutations, so it hit an empty database. Reproduced both ways from this
worktree at this tree state:

  $ source <fixture.env>; bunx vitest run tests/unit/services/reports/incomeStatementDisclosureDb.test.ts
    Test Files  1 failed (1)
         Tests  7 failed | 1 passed (8)

  $ env -u DATABASE_URL bunx vitest run tests/unit/services/reports/incomeStatementDisclosureDb.test.ts
    Test Files  1 passed (1)
         Tests  1 passed | 7 skipped (8)

That file was the only failure in ~9.5k tests. `bun run test:unit` in a shell with
no DATABASE_URL passes: 784 files passed / 36 skipped, 9320 tests passed / 234
skipped, exit 0 (full output: scratchpad/k012-unit3.log). Run the unit suite in a
clean shell; do not carry the integration fixture env into it.
